  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till Centre for Economics and Foreign Policy Studies EDAM 2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Centre for Economics and Foreign Policy Studies EDAM 2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den planerade utvecklingsinsatsen syftar till att st&#xf6;tta oberoende informationsspridning i Turkiet f&#xf6;r att bidra till en mer pluralistisk s&#xe5;dan. P&#xe5; s&#xe5; vis ses insatsen vara ett st&#xf6;d till &#xf6;kad yttrandefrihet och ambassaden bed&#xf6;mer att insatsen p&#xe5; sikt kan bidra till &#xf6;kat ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande g&#xe4;llande yttrandefrihet p&#xe5; n&#xe4;tet och demokrati. Det planerade svenska st&#xf6;det till Centre for Economics and Foreign Policy Studies (EDAM) bereds som ett projektst&#xf6;d utifr&#xe5;n syftet att st&#xf6;tta organisationens k&#xe4;rnverksamhet s&#xe5; att den kan fortl&#xf6;pa under r&#xe5;dande omst&#xe4;ndigheter.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The planned contribution aims to support dissemination of independent information in Turkey to enable a pluralistic environment of available independent information. The contribution is therefore supporting freedom of expression and the Embassy assesses that it in time can contribute to increased accountability regarding freedom of expression on-line and democracy. The planned Swedish support to Centre for Economics and Foreign Policy Studies (EDAM) is made through a project-grant with the aim to support EDAM&#x2019;s core activities so that the think tank can continue to undertake its work under the current circumstances.</narrative>
  </description>
